Article 19

(1) The Regional Government establishes partnership with the business sector in the protection of women and children from violence and discrimination.

(2) Partnership as referred to in paragraph (1) is conducted through:

a. notification of employment opportunity information for women victims of violence;

b. education and training for women victims of violence;

c. educational assistance for women and children victims of violence who have been withdrawn from their education;

d. fostering and enhancing economic independence of women victims of violence; and

e. elimination of the worst forms of child labor.

(3) Partnership as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2), shall be set forth in the form of agreement in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

Article 6

Women and children victims of acts of violence and discrimination shall receive the following rights:

a. the right to have their dignity and worth as human beings respected; b. the right to health and psychological recovery from the suffering experienced by victims;
c. the right to determine their own decisions;
d. the right to obtain information;
e. the right to confidentiality;
f. the right to social rehabilitation;
g. the right to complaint handling;
h. the right of victims and their families to obtain facilitation in the judicial process;
i. the right to assistance;
j. the right to respect for survival, growth and development;
k. the right to basic services;
l. the right to equal protection;
m. the right to be free from various stigma; and
n. the right to obtain freedom.

Article 2

Protection of women and children from acts of violence and discrimination is organized based on the principles of:

a. respect for human rights;
b. justice and gender equality;
c. non-discrimination;
d. victim protection;
e. empowerment; and
f. integration.

Article 18

(1) In order to achieve the objectives of protection of women and children from violence as referred to in Article 3, the Regional Government cooperates with:

a. the Government;
b. the Provincial Government;
c. Other Regency/City Governments;
d. Village Governments;
e. the Community; and
f. Mass Media.
(2) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) may be set forth in the form of Joint Agreement in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

