Article 9

Obligations and responsibilities in providing protection to women and children from acts of violence and discrimination are the joint responsibility of:

a. Regional Government;
b. Village Government;
c. Community; and
d. Family.

CHAPTER III

PREVENTION OF ACTS OF VIOLENCE AND DISCRIMINATION Article 4

(1) To prevent acts of violence and discrimination against women and children, the Regional Government conducts empowerment and awareness to families, parents, and the community by providing information, guidance and/or counseling.

(2) In addition to empowerment and awareness as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government undertakes the following efforts: a. increase the quantity and quality of education both formal and non-formal and informal;

b. opening accessibility to obtain education, training, funding, income enhancement and social services;

c. facilitate the provision of employment opportunities for women; d. encourage community participation and concern for the prevention of protection of women and children from acts of violence and discrimination;

e. build and provide a complete and easily accessible information system;

f. build networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, educational institutions and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care for women and children; and

g. open an integrated service system for the protection of women and children from acts of violence and discrimination in every village.

Article 18

(1) In order to achieve the objectives of protection of women and children from violence as referred to in Article 3, the Regional Government cooperates with:

a. the Government;
b. the Provincial Government;
c. Other Regency/City Governments;
d. Village Governments;
e. the Community; and
f. Mass Media.
(2) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) may be set forth in the form of Joint Agreement in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

6.9.text:
Article 6

Women and children victims of acts of violence and discrimination shall receive the following rights:

a. the right to have their dignity and worth as human beings respected; b. the right to health and psychological recovery from the suffering experienced by victims;
c. the right to determine their own decisions;
d. the right to obtain information;
e. the right to confidentiality;
f. the right to social rehabilitation;
g. the right to complaint handling;
h. the right of victims and their families to obtain facilitation in the judicial process;
i. the right to assistance;
j. the right to respect for survival, growth and development;
k. the right to basic services;
l. the right to equal protection;
m. the right to be free from various stigma; and
n. the right to obtain freedom.

Article 11

Obligations and responsibilities of the Village Government as referred to in Article 10 letter b, include:

a. implementing policies for the protection of women and children from acts of violence and discrimination established by the government;
b. conducting cooperation in the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence and discrimination; c. providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence and discrimination;
d. allocating budget for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence and discrimination according to village financial capacity;
e. fostering and supervising the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence and discrimination; and f. encouraging and increasing community participation.

Article 8

(1) Forms of services provided to women and children victims of acts of violence and discrimination as referred to in Article 7 include:

a. complaint services;
b. health services;
c. legal aid services;
d. repatriation services;
e. rehabilitation and social reintegration services; and f. education services for children who are victims of acts of violence and discrimination.
(2) Forms of services as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented in accordance with minimum service standards established by the government and implemented by Regional Apparatus whose duties and functions are in the field of:
a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. education;
d. women's empowerment and child protection; and e. mental and spiritual matters.
(3) Further provisions regarding procedures for services for handling women and children from acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

Article 12

(1) The community shall participate in the protection of women and children victims of violence and discrimination, either individually or in groups.

(2) The role of the community as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out by individuals, women and child protection institutions, social welfare institutions, community organizations, educational institutions, mass media, and the business community.

(3) The role of the community in the implementation of protection of women and children as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out by:

a. providing information through socialization and education regarding the protection of women and children from acts of violence and discrimination;
b. providing input in the formulation of policies related to the protection of women and children from acts of violence and discrimination;
c. reporting to the authorities if violations of acts of violence and discrimination against women and children occur;
d. playing an active role in the process of rehabilitation and social reintegration for women and children victims of acts of violence and discrimination;
e. conducting monitoring and supervision of the protection of women and children from acts of violence and discrimination; f. providing facilities and infrastructure in order to support the protection of women and children from acts of violence and discrimination;
g. playing an active role in eliminating negative labeling of women and children victims of acts of violence and discrimination; and
h. providing space for women and children to participate and express their opinions.

CHAPTER III

PREVENTION OF ACTS OF VIOLENCE AND DISCRIMINATION Article 4

