g. open an integrated service system for the protection of women and children from acts of violence and discrimination in every village.

Article 11

Obligations and responsibilities of the Village Government as referred to in Article 10 letter b, include:

a. implementing policies for the protection of women and children from acts of violence and discrimination established by the government;
b. conducting cooperation in the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence and discrimination; c. providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence and discrimination;
d. allocating budget for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence and discrimination according to village financial capacity;
e. fostering and supervising the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence and discrimination; and f. encouraging and increasing community participation.

Article 19

(1) The Regional Government establishes partnership with the business sector in the protection of women and children from violence and discrimination.

(2) Partnership as referred to in paragraph (1) is conducted through:

a. notification of employment opportunity information for women victims of violence;

b. education and training for women victims of violence;

c. educational assistance for women and children victims of violence who have been withdrawn from their education;

d. fostering and enhancing economic independence of women victims of violence; and

e. elimination of the worst forms of child labor.

(3) Partnership as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2), shall be set forth in the form of agreement in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

